cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ProForma-20Q, please cite the benchmark and its companion paper."
title: "ProForma-20Q: A Benchmark for Joint Probabilistic Forecasting of Quarterly Financial Statements"
abstract: >-
  ProForma-20Q defines a public, reproducible benchmark task for joint
  probabilistic forecasting of the complete quarterly financial statements of
  U.S. public firms at horizons of 1 to 20 quarters. Given WRDS credentials, one
  command rebuilds the exact data environment and evaluation. The benchmark ships
  the data build, splits, targets, regularization transform, evaluation protocol,
  submission format, and reference baselines -- but no data and no model.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/forma-lab-mccombs/proforma-20q"
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - financial-statement-forecasting
  - probabilistic-forecasting
  - Compustat
# NOTE: authorship is intentionally minimal here so the repository is trivial to
# mirror anonymously for double-blind review. Populate authors/preferred-citation
# at (de-anonymized) public release.
authors:
  - name: "The ProForma-20Q Authors"
preferred-citation:
  type: conference-paper
  title: "ProForma-20Q (ICAIF '26)"
  year: 2026
  authors:
    - name: "The ProForma-20Q Authors"
